Package: kvmweb
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8),
 python3-flask | python3-pip,
 python3-libvirt,
 python3-pam,
 python3-bcrypt,
 libvirt-daemon-system,
 qemu-kvm,
 virtinst,
 openssl
Recommends: qemu-utils
Maintainer: kvmweb <kvmweb@localhost>
Description: Lightweight KVM web management interface
 kvmweb is a self-hosted web UI for managing KVM/QEMU virtual machines
 via libvirt. Features include VM lifecycle control (start, stop, reboot,
 suspend), live dashboard with host stats, VM creation via virt-install,
 storage pool and network visibility, PAM-based authentication, and
 HTTPS with a self-signed certificate.
 .
 Accessible at https://HOST:8080 after installation.
Homepage: https://github.com/netanelcyber/penuX
